- op: discuss  # 95ab
  at: '2026-05-01T19:26:50Z'  # 95ab
  by: agent  # 95ab
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 95ab
  clock: 2  # 95ab
  nonce: 95ab  # 95ab
  message: "AUDIT VERDICT: DOCUMENT + EXTEND (sibling-boolean pattern, mirroring WI-rigun/WI-tizij/WI-zimum).\n\nFOUR LEAKAGE TESTS — tier as a whole:\n- Test 1 (Property derivability): The four roles inside tier=2 (internal_dep / examples / configs / tests) are NOT all derivable from tier=2 alone. is_test_file already exists (WI-rigun) — that's the existing precedent for spinning role-questions out of the tier value. examples/configs are NOT yet split out; consumers asking 'is this an example?' or 'is this a config?' have no way to answer from Symbol fields. **PARTIAL LEAKAGE on tier=2 only.**\n- Test 2 (Apex/peer): tier=2 is ordinal-shaped throughout — never used as 'top type' AND 'subtype' simultaneously. **PASSES.**\n- Test 3 (Construct vs relationship): tier names a supply-chain ROLE; not a syntactic construct. **PASSES.**\n- Test 4 (Mechanism vs category): tier itself is a clean category (where in the supply chain). **PASSES.**\n\nVERDICT: tier itself is clean as an ordinal axis. The localized smell is the four-way conflation inside tier=2 — and the codebase has already established the right-shaped fix: spin role-questions out as sibling booleans on Symbol (is_test_file from WI-rigun, is_generated_file from WI-tizij, is_exported from WI-zimum). Extending this pattern with is_example_file + is_config_file is the natural completion.\n\nWhy NOT splitting tier numerically (e.g., 2.1=internal_dep, 2.2=example, 2.3=config): breaks the ordinal 'lower = higher priority' semantics and forces every consumer that today writes 'tier <= 2' to handle floats or new sub-tiers.\n\nWhy NOT collapsing tier+role into a single supply_chain_role string field: would require migrating every consumer of the integer ordinal (a wide blast radius) for a benefit (string-typing) the existing booleans already provide cleanly.\n\nFOLLOW-UP CODE: filing WI-(new) for the actual is_example_file + is_config_file additions + supply_chain.py wire-up + 'is this an internal_dep?' consumer pattern documentation. The sibling booleans are mechanical to add.\n\nRE-EVALUATION TRIGGER: if a consumer needs a FIFTH role distinction inside tier=2 (e.g., 'is this a build script?'), revisit whether the proliferating booleans should consolidate into a string-valued supply_chain_role. The current ceiling is ~4 booleans; beyond that the per-boolean overhead exceeds the typing-clarity benefit."  # 95ab
